THE CUT, WHICH IS THE SAME FOR BOTH

Both families are subset to Latin — Basic, Supplement, Extended-A and Extended-B,
general punctuation, currency, and the f-ligatures — and to the OpenType features
running text actually uses: kern, liga, clig, calt, ccmp, locl, mark, mkmk, rlig.
Dropping the rest is where most of the weight goes; EB Garamond ships small caps,
old-style figures and swashes that a lyric will never ask for, and they cost 460 KB
across four files.

That is 706 KB for eight faces. The eight upstream files they were cut from are
about 4 MB.

The cost is that both families' Greek and Cyrillic are gone, along with those
extra figure and small-cap sets. A note written in either script renders in the
system font instead, because Android falls back glyph by glyph. Deliberate, and
reversible by re-cutting from upstream.

Source Serif 4 was bundled here between 2026-09-08 and the same day, and was
removed for being too close to Literata to be a choice. It is worth recording why
it was handled differently while it was here: its name table declares `with
Reserved Font Name 'Source'`, so under OFL clause 3 it could not be cut down and
still be called Source Serif, and it shipped unmodified at 892 KB. If it or any
other RFN font is ever wanted, that is the constraint.


